IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tlca-dates`

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) -- the child abuse provisions: the removal of the limitation period for actions arising from
-- the sexual or serious physical abuse of a minor (s 5B, with ss 2(1), 5A, 26(1A), 26A, 38, 38A and 39(1) around it), and
-- the setting aside of child abuse claims settled after their time had run (s 5C). These are Tasmania's equivalents of the
-- limitation removals other Australian jurisdictions made after the Royal Commission into Institutional Responses to Child
-- Sexual Abuse; the organisational liability amendments of the same reform are in Part 10C of the Civil Liability Act 2002
-- (Tas), a different Act that this folder cannot import (see NOTES.md).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in tlca-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "must not be brought
-- after", "may not be granted", "nothing in this Act enables", "cannot seek to recover", "if a court orders" not met, a
-- "while" that does not hold); NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
-- The court's judgments ("just and reasonable", "interest(s) of justice", "ought to have known") are inputs.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1974: child abuse claims`

§§ `Days the Act fixes`

-- s 5B was inserted by the Limitation Amendment Act 2017 (No. 52 of 2017), "Applied:01 Jul 2018" in the history note;
-- the same day is "the amendment day" of s 38A(1) and "the day on which section 5B commenced" (s 5C(1)).
`the day section 5B commenced` MEANS `the day` 1 7 2018

-- s 39(1) speaks of "the commencement of this Act": s 1(2), "This Act shall commence on 1st January 1975".
`the day this Act commenced` MEANS `the day` 1 1 1975

-- A serial day later than any real day, for a suspension that has not ended.
`the endless serial` MEANS 100000000

§§ `s 5B -- what the abuse was`

-- s 5B(1): "the sexual abuse, or serious physical abuse, of the person when the person was a minor"; (2): it "includes any
-- psychological abuse that arises from the sexual abuse or the serious physical abuse". s 5C(1) "child abuse" names the
-- same three. "Sexual abuse", "serious physical abuse" and "psychological abuse" are not defined: asked as facts.
DECLARE `What the abuse was` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse`
    `physical abuse that was not serious`
    `psychological abuse alone, or neglect`

GIVEN a IS A `What the abuse was`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abuse is of a kind ss 5B and 5C name` a IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `physical abuse that was not serious` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `psychological abuse alone, or neglect` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 5B(1)(a) "an action for damages for personal injury to a person arising from or related to the ... abuse ... of the
-- person"; (b) "an action for damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 in respect of the death of a person arising from
-- or related to the ... abuse ... of the person". Either way the abused person is the injured or deceased person.
DECLARE `What the action is` IS ONE OF
    `damages for personal injury to the person who was abused`
    `damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for the death of the person who was abused`
    `damages for injury to someone other than the person who was abused`
    `another kind of action`

GIVEN k IS A `What the action is`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is one s 5B names` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `damages for personal injury to the person who was abused` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for the death of the person who was abused` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 5A(3), (4): an action for damages for negligence, nuisance or breach of duty that include damages for personal
-- injuries, and a Fatal Accidents Act action, take 3 years from the date of discoverability. A claim for injury to someone
-- other than the abused person (a parent's own nervous shock, say) is still such an action. "Breach of duty" is read to
-- include an intentional wrong such as assault (fork F6).
GIVEN k IS A `What the action is`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is one s 5A names` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `another kind of action` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 5B -- no limitation period`

-- s 5B(1): "Despite section 5A and section 26A -- (a) ... (b) ... may be brought at any time." A grant limited in its own
-- wording: where the facts fall outside it, the section is silent and s 5A governs (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its
-- own wording; the case falls outside the limit). s 38A(2): the Act as amended in 2018 "applies in relation to an action
-- in respect of a personal injury -- (a) whether the cause of action accrued before, on or after the amendment day; and
-- (b) whether or not a period of limitation under the Act, as in force before the amendment day -- (i) has, before that
-- day, expired": so s 5B reaches abuse long past.
-- s 38: "This Act does not apply to any action ... for which a period of limitation is prescribed by any other enactment"
-- (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
-- s 39(1): "Nothing in this Act enables any action to be brought that was barred before the commencement of this Act".
-- s 5B is "despite section 5A and section 26A" but not despite s 39, and s 38A(2)(b) speaks only of periods "under the
-- Act" (this Act). A flat negative: JUST FALSE for an action already barred before 1 January 1975 under the law then in
-- force (fork F2; finding 1).
GIVEN `the action` IS A `What the action is`
      `the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was`
      `the person was a minor when abused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury or death arose from or related to the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act sets the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action was barred before 1 January 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B -- the action may be brought at any time` `the action` `the abuse` `the person was a minor when abused` `the injury or death arose from or related to the abuse` `another Act sets the period` `the action was barred before 1 January 1975` MEANS
    IF `another Act sets the period`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the action was barred before 1 January 1975`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `s 5B(1) reaches it`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `s 5B(1) reaches it` MEANS
                `the action is one s 5B names` `the action`
            AND `the abuse is of a kind ss 5B and 5C name` `the abuse`
            AND `the person was a minor when abused`
            AND `the injury or death arose from or related to the abuse`

§§ `s 5A(5) and s 38A(3) -- the extension to 6 years`

-- s 5A(5): "A judge may extend the period of limitation referred to in subsection (3) to the expiration of 6 years
-- commencing on the date of discoverability if he or she considers that, in the circumstances of the case, it is just and
-- reasonable to do so." s 38A(3): an extension "may not be granted under section 5A(5) ... in relation to a cause of action
-- that accrued before that day, if the date of discoverability occurred more than 3 years before that day": before
-- 1 July 2015 (fork F3). "May not be granted": JUST FALSE; otherwise JUST TRUE (the judge may, if just and reasonable).
GIVEN `the cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of discoverability` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A(5) -- a judge may give 6 years` `the cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018` `the date of discoverability` MEANS
    IF `the cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018` AND (`the date of discoverability` `falls before` (`the same day` (-3) `years on from` `the day section 5B commenced`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 26A -- the suspension while a relevant person`

-- s 26A(4): "A person is a relevant person -- (a) while the person is a minor and is not in the custody of a capable
-- parent; or (b) while the person is a person to whom section 2(2)(b) applies for a continuous period of 28 days or more
-- and either -- (i) there is no legal representative ...; or (ii) the legal representative ... is in a close relationship
-- with the intended defendant." s 26A(1): a "capable parent" is a parent "(b) who is not under a disability; and (c) who
-- is not the intended defendant or a parent who is in a close relationship with the intended defendant"; s 26A(2)(a): a
-- parent is in a close relationship if "the parent, or another parent, may be directly or indirectly influenced by the
-- intended defendant not to bring an action". For a child abused at home this is the usual case: the abusing parent is
-- the intended defendant, and the other parent may be in a close relationship with him or her.
-- "While": JUST FALSE when neither head holds.
GIVEN `I am a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in the custody of a parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that parent is under a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that parent is the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been incapable by mental disorder for a continuous 28 days or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone not the person I would sue has legal authority to sue for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that representative may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(4) -- I am now a relevant person` `I am a minor` `I am in the custody of a parent` `that parent is under a disability` `that parent is the person I would sue` `a parent may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` `I have been incapable by mental disorder for a continuous 28 days or more` `someone not the person I would sue has legal authority to sue for me` `that representative may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` MEANS
    IF `head (a) holds` OR `head (b) holds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the parent is a capable parent` MEANS
                `I am in the custody of a parent`
            AND (NOT `that parent is under a disability`)
            AND (NOT `that parent is the person I would sue`)
            AND (NOT `a parent may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue`)
        `head (a) holds` MEANS `I am a minor` AND (NOT `the parent is a capable parent`)
        `head (b) holds` MEANS
                `I have been incapable by mental disorder for a continuous 28 days or more`
            AND ((NOT `someone not the person I would sue has legal authority to sue for me`) OR `that representative may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue`)

-- Why a person was a relevant person during one spell.
DECLARE `Why the clock stopped` IS ONE OF
    `I was a minor not in the custody of a capable parent`
    `I was incapable by mental disorder with no independent legal representative`

-- One spell during which the person was a relevant person. s 26A(3): "The running of the limitation period ... is
-- suspended for each period in which the person is a relevant person." The days of the spell on or after the date of
-- discoverability are added to the last day, if the spell begins on or before the last day as it stands (fork F5). A
-- minor's spell ends at the latest on the day before the 18th birthday (fork F4). An incapacity spell counts only if it
-- lasts "a continuous period of 28 days or more" (one not yet ended is counted), and then the whole spell is suspended
-- (fork F5). One spell only: an encoding with two spells is the claimant's baseline beside this one.
DECLARE `The spell` HAS
    `there was a spell`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `why`                IS A `Why the clock stopped`
    `spell began`        IS A DATE
    `spell has ended`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `spell ended`        IS A DATE

GIVEN s IS A `The spell`, `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last serial of` s `for birth on` `the birth day` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `why`
    WHEN `I was a minor not in the custody of a capable parent` THEN min `the given end` (DATE_SERIAL (`the 18th birthday for birth on` `the birth day`) MINUS 1)
    OTHERWISE `the given end`
    WHERE
        `the given end` MEANS
            IF s's `spell has ended`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL (s's `spell ended`)
            ELSE `the endless serial`

GIVEN s IS A `The spell`, `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spell counts` s `for birth on` `the birth day` IF
        s's `there was a spell`
    AND `long enough`
    WHERE
        `long enough` MEANS
            CONSIDER s's `why`
            WHEN `I was incapable by mental disorder with no independent legal representative` THEN
                (`the last serial of` s `for birth on` `the birth day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (s's `spell began`)) PLUS 1 AT LEAST 28
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The last day (as a serial) after the spell: the ordinary last day, plus the days of the spell from the later of its
-- first day and the start of the period, if that is not after the ordinary last day.
GIVEN s IS A `The spell`, `the birth day` IS A DATE, `the period start` IS A DATE, `the ordinary last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last serial with` s `for birth on` `the birth day` `from` `the period start` `ordinarily ending` `the ordinary last` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the spell counts` s `for birth on` `the birth day`)
    THEN DATE_SERIAL `the ordinary last`
    ELSE IF `the spell's last` LESS THAN `the counted first`
         THEN DATE_SERIAL `the ordinary last`
         ELSE IF `the counted first` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the ordinary last`
              THEN DATE_SERIAL `the ordinary last`
              ELSE IF `the spell's last` AT LEAST `the endless serial`
                   THEN `the endless serial`
                   ELSE DATE_SERIAL `the ordinary last` PLUS (`the spell's last` MINUS `the counted first`) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        `the spell's last` MEANS `the last serial of` s `for birth on` `the birth day`
        `the counted first` MEANS max (DATE_SERIAL (s's `spell began`)) (DATE_SERIAL `the period start`)

§§ `The time limit for an abuse claim`

DECLARE `The time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period: the action may be brought at any time (s 5B)`
    `the last day to bring the action is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no last day yet: the time is suspended and the suspension has not ended (s 26A)`
    `barred before 1975, and this Act does not revive it (s 39(1))`
    `another Act's time limit applies (s 38)`
    `not an action this encoding answers`

-- One abuse claim, as the person bringing it states it.
DECLARE `The abuse claim` HAS
    `the action`                          IS A `What the action is`
    `the abuse`                           IS A `What the abuse was`
    `abused as a minor`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from or related to the abuse`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `another Act's period`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `barred before 1975`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of discoverability`             IS A DATE
    `judge extended to 6 years`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `accrued before 1 July 2018`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `birth day`                           IS A DATE
    `spell`                               IS A `The spell`

-- s 5A(3): "must not be brought after the expiration of 3 years commencing on the date of discoverability"; (5): 6 years
-- if a judge extends it, unless s 38A(3) forbids. s 26(1A): "This section [s 26, disability] does not apply to a cause of
-- action to which section 5A or 5B applies": being a child when abused gives no s 26 extension; only s 26A can stop the
-- clock (finding 3).
GIVEN c IS A `The abuse claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years allowed for` c MEANS
    IF c's `judge extended to 6 years` AND (`s 5A(5) -- a judge may give 6 years` (c's `accrued before 1 July 2018`) (c's `date of discoverability`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN 6
    ELSE 3

GIVEN c IS A `The abuse claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last serial for` c MEANS
    `the last serial with` (c's `spell`) `for birth on` (c's `birth day`) `from` (c's `date of discoverability`) `ordinarily ending` (`the final day of` (`the years allowed for` c) `years commencing on` (c's `date of discoverability`))

GIVEN c IS A `The abuse claim`
GIVETH A `The time limit`
`the time limit for the abuse claim` c MEANS
    IF c's `another Act's period`
    THEN `another Act's time limit applies (s 38)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the action is one s 5A names` (c's `the action`))
         THEN `not an action this encoding answers`
         ELSE IF c's `barred before 1975`
              THEN `barred before 1975, and this Act does not revive it (s 39(1))`
              ELSE IF `s 5B -- the action may be brought at any time` (c's `the action`) (c's `the abuse`) (c's `abused as a minor`) (c's `arose from or related to the abuse`) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   THEN `no limitation period: the action may be brought at any time (s 5B)`
                   ELSE IF `the last serial for` c AT LEAST `the endless serial`
                        THEN `no last day yet: the time is suspended and the suspension has not ended (s 26A)`
                        ELSE `the last day to bring the action is` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (`the last serial for` c))

§§ `The time bar as a regulative rule`

-- "must not be brought after the expiration of" the period (s 5A(3)): what the plaintiff must do to keep the action. The
-- rule starts on a day and allows the days to the last day; FULFILLED means in time, anything else too late. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Who acts` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`
    `the other party to the settlement`

DECLARE `What is done` IS ONE OF
    `bring the action`
    `seek to recover what it paid because the agreement is void`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Who acts` `What is done`
`the plaintiff must bring the action within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    MUST `bring the action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the limitation period has expired: s 5A(3) says the action must not be brought after it"

GIVEN `the time of bringing it` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Who acts` `What is done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bringing it at` `the time of bringing it` `keeps` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of bringing it`), (EVENT `the plaintiff` `bring the action` `the time of bringing it`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether an action brought on a day is in time. JUST FALSE after the last day ("must not be brought after") and for an
-- action barred before 1975 (s 39(1)); JUST TRUE where no period applies or the suspension has not ended; NOTHING under
-- another Act or outside the encoding (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
GIVEN `the day it is brought` IS A DATE, `the limit` IS A `The time limit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an action brought on` `the day it is brought` `is in time under` `the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `no limitation period: the action may be brought at any time (s 5B)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no last day yet: the time is suspended and the suspension has not ended (s 26A)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `barred before 1975, and this Act does not revive it (s 39(1))` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the last day to bring the action is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `bringing it at` (`the number of days from` `the base` `until` `the day it is brought`) `keeps` (`the plaintiff must bring the action within` (`the number of days from` `the base` `until` `the final day`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHERE
            `the base` MEANS `the sooner of` `the day it is brought` `and` `the final day`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 5C(1) -- child abuse, and a previously settled claim`

-- s 5C(1): "child abuse means -- (a) sexual abuse, or serious physical abuse, of a child; and (b) any psychological abuse
-- of the child that arises from the sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child -- but does not include an act
-- that is lawful at the time at which it occurs". A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when it does not hold.
GIVEN `the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was`
      `I was a child when abused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was lawful when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5C(1) -- it is child abuse` `the abuse` `I was a child when abused` `the act was lawful when it occurred` MEANS
    IF `the abuse is of a kind ss 5B and 5C name` `the abuse`
       AND `I was a child when abused`
       AND (NOT `the act was lawful when it occurred`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 5C(1): "previously settled relevant right of action means a relevant right of action [a right of action in respect of
-- child abuse] that was settled before the day on which section 5B commenced but after a limitation period applying
-- before that day to the right of action had expired". s 5C(2): "An action may be brought on a previously settled relevant
-- right of action if a relevant court, by order on application, sets aside the agreement effecting the settlement, on the
-- grounds that it is in the interest of justice to do so." s 5C(8): "This section does not apply in relation to an
-- agreement effecting a settlement that is an offer of redress accepted under section 42 of the National Redress Scheme
-- for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 of the Commonwealth." Each "does not reach" answer is the text's own no
-- (a "means" definition, a flat "does not apply").
DECLARE `What I can do about the settlement` IS ONE OF
    `s 5C does not apply: the settlement was an offer of redress accepted under the National Redress Scheme (s 5C(8))`
    `s 5C does not reach it: what happened is not child abuse as s 5C(1) defines it`
    `s 5C does not reach it: the claim was settled on or after 1 July 2018`
    `s 5C does not reach it: no limitation period had expired when the claim was settled`
    `you may apply to a court to set the settlement aside; it will if that is in the interests of justice (s 5C(2), (3))`
    `the settlement is set aside: you may bring the action (s 5C(2)), with no limitation period if s 5B applies`

GIVEN `the abuse` IS A `What the abuse was`
      `I was a child when abused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was lawful when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the settlement` IS A DATE
      `a limitation period had expired before the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was an accepted National Redress Scheme offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has set the settlement aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What I can do about the settlement`
`s 5C(1), (2), (8) -- what I can do about the settlement` `the abuse` `I was a child when abused` `the act was lawful when it occurred` `the day of the settlement` `a limitation period had expired before the settlement` `it was an accepted National Redress Scheme offer` `a court has set the settlement aside` MEANS
    IF `it was an accepted National Redress Scheme offer`
    THEN `s 5C does not apply: the settlement was an offer of redress accepted under the National Redress Scheme (s 5C(8))`
    ELSE IF NOT (`s 5C(1) -- it is child abuse` `the abuse` `I was a child when abused` `the act was lawful when it occurred` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN `s 5C does not reach it: what happened is not child abuse as s 5C(1) defines it`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the day of the settlement` `falls before` `the day section 5B commenced`)
              THEN `s 5C does not reach it: the claim was settled on or after 1 July 2018`
              ELSE IF NOT (`a limitation period had expired before the settlement`)
                   THEN `s 5C does not reach it: no limitation period had expired when the claim was settled`
                   ELSE IF `a court has set the settlement aside`
                        THEN `the settlement is set aside: you may bring the action (s 5C(2)), with no limitation period if s 5B applies`
                        ELSE `you may apply to a court to set the settlement aside; it will if that is in the interests of justice (s 5C(2), (3))`

§§ `s 5C(4) -- which agreements become void`

-- s 5C(4): "If a court orders under subsection (2) that an agreement effecting a settlement be set aside, so much of the
-- agreement, and any other agreement (apart from a contract of insurance) relating to the settlement, is, despite any Act,
-- law or rule of law, void to the extent to which it relates to the child abuse to which the cause of action relates."
-- "If a court orders": no order, nothing is void under (4) (JUST FALSE kind). "Apart from a contract of insurance": a
-- flat exception. An agreement not relating to the settlement is outside the subsection (NOTHING-kind: limited in its own
-- wording). "To the extent to which it relates to the child abuse": wholly if solely about it, in part if partly, not at
-- all if not (fork F8).
DECLARE `Which agreement` IS ONE OF
    `the agreement that settled my claim`
    `another agreement relating to the settlement, such as a deed of release or a confidentiality agreement`
    `a contract of insurance`
    `an agreement that does not relate to the settlement`

DECLARE `How far it relates to the abuse` IS ONE OF
    `only to the child abuse`
    `partly to the child abuse`
    `not to the child abuse`

DECLARE `What s 5C(4) does to it` IS ONE OF
    `it is wholly void`
    `it is void to the extent it relates to the child abuse`
    `it is not void under s 5C(4): no court has set the settlement aside`
    `it is not void under s 5C(4): a contract of insurance is excepted`
    `it is not void under s 5C(4): it does not relate to the child abuse`
    `s 5C(4) does not reach an agreement that does not relate to the settlement`

GIVEN `a court has set the settlement aside` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement` IS A `Which agreement`
      `how far` IS A `How far it relates to the abuse`
GIVETH A `What s 5C(4) does to it`
`s 5C(4) -- what becomes of the agreement` `a court has set the settlement aside` `the agreement` `how far` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a court has set the settlement aside`)
    THEN `it is not void under s 5C(4): no court has set the settlement aside`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the agreement`
         WHEN `a contract of insurance` THEN `it is not void under s 5C(4): a contract of insurance is excepted`
         WHEN `an agreement that does not relate to the settlement` THEN `s 5C(4) does not reach an agreement that does not relate to the settlement`
         OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `how far`
            WHEN `only to the child abuse` THEN `it is wholly void`
            WHEN `partly to the child abuse` THEN `it is void to the extent it relates to the child abuse`
            OTHERWISE `it is not void under s 5C(4): it does not relate to the child abuse`

§§ `s 5C(5) -- no recovery of what was paid`

-- s 5C(5): "A party to an agreement that is wholly or partly void under subsection (4) cannot seek to recover an amount
-- paid by or in respect of the party under the agreement on the basis that the agreement is void to that extent." A
-- prohibition on the other party, with no time limit: written as SHANT, and run against the step of seeking to recover.
-- It speaks only of recovery "on the basis that the agreement is void"; recovery on another basis is outside it (NOTHING-
-- kind: a prohibition limited in its own wording), as is an agreement not made void (fork F9).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Who acts` `What is done`
`s 5C(5) -- the other party shall not seek to recover` MEANS
    PARTY `the other party to the settlement`
    SHANT `seek to recover what it paid because the agreement is void`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the other party to the settlement` BECAUSE "s 5C(5): a party to an agreement made void under s 5C(4) cannot seek to recover an amount paid under it on the basis that it is void"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `seeking to recover breaks the s 5C(5) bar` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 5C(5) -- the other party shall not seek to recover` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the other party to the settlement` `seek to recover what it paid because the agreement is void` 1))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `On what ground it would recover` IS ONE OF
    `because the agreement is void under s 5C`
    `on some other ground`

GIVEN `what s 5C(4) did` IS A `What s 5C(4) does to it`
      `the ground` IS A `On what ground it would recover`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5C(5) -- the other party may recover what it paid` `what s 5C(4) did` `the ground` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is wholly or partly void`
    THEN CONSIDER `the ground`
         WHEN `because the agreement is void under s 5C` THEN
            IF `seeking to recover breaks the s 5C(5) bar`
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the agreement is wholly or partly void` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what s 5C(4) did`
            WHEN `it is wholly void` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `it is void to the extent it relates to the child abuse` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 5C(6), (7) -- taking the earlier payment into account`

-- s 5C(6): a court hearing the action "may, if it is satisfied that it is just and reasonable to do so when awarding
-- damages ..., take into account any amount, paid under an agreement that is wholly or partly void under subsection (4),
-- to the extent to which the amount relates to the child abuse". (7): "half of the total of all amounts paid under an
-- agreement is taken to be the amount relating to the child abuse ..., if the agreement -- (a) does not relate solely to
-- the child abuse; and (b) does not expressly indicate the extent to which the agreement and amounts paid under it relate
-- to the child abuse." The answer is the most the court may take into account; whether it does is its judgment, and an
-- agreement solely about the abuse gives the whole, one that expressly indicates a part gives that part (fork F10).
GIVEN `the total of all amounts paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement related solely to the child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement expressly indicated the part for the child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part it indicated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5C(6), (7) -- the most the court may take into account` `the total of all amounts paid` `the agreement related solely to the child abuse` `the agreement expressly indicated the part for the child abuse` `the part it indicated` MEANS
    IF `the agreement related solely to the child abuse`
    THEN `the total of all amounts paid`
    ELSE IF `the agreement expressly indicated the part for the child abuse`
         THEN `the part it indicated`
         ELSE `the total of all amounts paid` DIVIDED BY 2
